<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">PentestBlueprint</a><span>/</span><a href="/dark-codex">The Dark Codex</a><span>/</span><span>RustScan</span></nav>
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">THE DARK CODEX / RECONNAISSANCE</p><h1>RustScan<span>.</span></h1><p class="lead">Fast TCP port discovery with Nmap handoff. RustScan is useful for identifying candidate TCP ports quickly, then handing those ports to Nmap for deeper service inspection.</p></header>
<img class="hero-img" src="/images/dark-codex/rustscan.png" alt="RustScan Dark Codex cover" loading="eager" width="768" height="256" />
<div class="note"><strong>Scope:</strong> These examples are intended for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. Replace placeholders with lab values. CLI options can change between releases; check each tool's <code>--help</code> output.</div>
<div class="body-grid"><article>
<section class="section" id="commands"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FIELD COMMANDS</p><h2>Commands you'll actually use</h2><div class="examples"><div class="example"><h3>Basic discovery</h3><p>Scan a target for open TCP ports.</p><pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;target&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Pass Nmap flags</h3><p>Discover ports and request Nmap service detection.</p><pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;target&gt; -- -sV</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Default scripts and versions</h3><p>Run Nmap default scripts and version checks on discovered ports.</p><pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;target&gt; -- -sC -sV</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Limited port range</h3><p>Focus on ports 1 through 1000.</p><pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;target&gt; -r 1-1000</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Reduce scan pressure</h3><p>Use a smaller batch size and a longer timeout.</p><pre><code>rustscan -a &lt;target&gt; -b 100 -t 2000 -- -sV</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Check supported flags</h3><p>Confirm available options for the installed version.</p><pre><code>rustscan --help</code></pre></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="concepts"><p class="eyebrow">02 / REMEMBER THIS</p><h2>Key concepts and flags</h2><div class="terms"><div class="term"><strong>Batch size</strong><p>-b controls concurrent batch size; lower values reduce load.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Timeout</strong><p>-t is the connection timeout in milliseconds in current CLI.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Nmap handoff</strong><p>Everything after -- is passed to Nmap.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="workflow"><p class="eyebrow">03 / FIELD NOTES</p><h2>Practical reminders</h2><ul><li>RustScan can be noisy; use conservative settings on fragile lab systems.</li><li>Confirm important findings with Nmap and record both outputs.</li></ul></section>
<section class="section sources" id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SOURCES & CREDITS</p><h2>Documentation and attribution</h2><p>This is an independently written PentestBlueprint quick reference informed by the official project documentation below. Tool names and trademarks belong to their respective projects; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/bee-san/RustScan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RustScan repository ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/bee-san/RustScan/wiki/Usage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RustScan usage wiki ↗</a></li></ul></section>
